<title>USA: U.S. corn growers back biotech crops.</title>
<headline>U.S. corn growers back biotech crops.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Corn Growers Association President Wallie Hardie Thursday said his group sees biotechnology as part of food security and a way to cut down on pesticide use.</p>
<p>&quot;Our position is that when the appropriate government agencies, whether it's here or abroad, approves a product and says it's safe, that we should go with it,&quot; Hardie said at a meeting of top U.S. corn and soybean growers.</p>
</text>
